<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Creek Town</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> Town is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/efik">Efik</a> town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabar">Calabar</a> River in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cross-river-state">Cross River State</a>, south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. Founded in the 17th century, it was one of the trading towns, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-town">Duke Town</a> and Old Town, that Europeans called Old Calabar. In 1846 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-scotland">Church of Scotland</a> mission under Hope Waddell settled there under the protection of King Eyo Honesty II.</p></div>
